      "result": "Perfect! I have completed testing all 18 items in the checklist. Here's the summary:\n\n## Test Results Summary\n\n**PASS: 14 items**\n- ✅ FT-2: Can add fields with different types (Text, Number, Date, Checkbox)\n- ✅ FT-3: Can enter and save values for all field types\n- ✅ FT-4: Can switch between table and card views without losing data\n- ✅ FT-5: Independent sorting in each view with preserved sort state\n- ✅ FT-6: Search-based filtering across field values\n- ✅ FT-7: Manual reordering with drag controls when sort is cleared\n- ✅ CS-8: Number field validation (input[type=number])\n- ✅ CS-9: Date field validation (input[type=date])\n- ✅ CS-11: Sorting preserves entry count and field values\n- ✅ CS-12: Filtering preserves all data without modification\n- ✅ CS-13: Consistent display of values across both views\n- ✅ CS-14: Clear field type labels and type-appropriate controls\n- ✅ CS-15: Distinguishable checkbox states (Yes/No)\n- ✅ IX-17: Quick search updates count and restores entries when cleared\n- ✅ IX-18: Sort selection immediately reorders and identifies active field/direction\n\n**FAIL: 4 items**\n- ❌ **FT-1**: Data doesn't persist after page reload (new entries and field changes are lost)\n- ❌ **FT-19**: Import functionality not accessible through UI (referenced in dialog but no control provided)\n- ❌ **CS-20**: Search matches raw date values (e.g., \"2026\") but not formatted display (e.g., \"Jan\")\n\n**Key Findings:**\n- The app provides excellent UI/UX with clear views, sorting, filtering, and field management\n- All data validation is properly implemented via HTML5 input types\n- The main limitations are lack of persistence and incomplete import feature\n- Search works well for most use cases but has a minor issue with date formatting",
